        "statement": "<p>A data logger dumps a flat buffer of readings. A report generator lays it out as <code>rows</code> lines, letting numpy infer the line width with the <code>-1</code> placeholder — and the report header needs the explicit width printed.</p><p>Implement <code>infer_shape(a, rows)</code>: return the full shape that <code>a.reshape(rows, -1)</code> produces, as a plain Python <b>list of two ints</b> <code>[rows, cols]</code>. Perform the reshape and read the shape back from the result — do not compute <code>cols</code> with your own division.</p>",
