        "title": "Images to Patches",
        "difficulty": "hard",
        "tags": [
          "numpy",
          "reshape",
          "transpose"
        ],
        "statement": "<p>A vision pipeline needs every <code>ph × pw</code> patch from a batch of grayscale images stored as a 3-D array <code>img</code> of shape <code>(N, H, W)</code>: N images of H rows by W columns.</p><p>Implement <code>to_patches(img, ph, pw)</code>: return an <code>int64</code> array of shape <code>(N, P, ph, pw)</code> with <code>P = (H//ph) * (W//pw)</code>. Patch <code>p</code> of image <code>n</code> covers rows <code>[i*ph, (i+1)*ph)</code> and columns <code>[j*pw, (j+1)*pw)</code> where <code>i = p // (W//pw)</code> and <code>j = p % (W//pw)</code> — row-major patch order. Use <b>only reshape and transpose</b>; no loops, no stride_tricks.</p>",
        "constraints": [
          "ph divides H and pw divides W, so there are no partial patches",
          "the output shape is exactly (N, (H//ph)*(W//pw), ph, pw), dtype int64",
          "no Python loops, no np.lib.stride_tricks: a reshape, a transpose, a reshape"
        ],
        "examples": [
          {
            "call": "to_patches(np.arange(16).reshape(1, 4, 4), 2, 2)",
            "returns": "array([[[[ 0,  1],\n         [ 4,  5]],\n\n        [[ 2,  3],\n         [ 6,  7]],\n\n        [[ 8,  9],\n         [12, 13]],\n\n        [[10, 11],\n         [14, 15]]]])",
